_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Missing empty-document check before `setAttributes()` on fetched user.**

When the identity exists but the associated user has been deleted (orphaned identity), `getDocument('users', ...)` returns an empty document. Calling `setAttributes()` with an empty array may leave `$user` in an inconsistent state, potentially bypassing the `isEmpty()` check at line 1679.

Compare with the pattern at lines 1658-1662 where `$userWithEmail` is checked for emptiness before calling `setAttributes()`.


<details>
<summary>Suggested fix:</summary>

```diff
 // If user is not found, check if there is an identity with the same email
 if ($user === false || $user->isEmpty()) {
     $identityWithMatchingEmail = $dbForProject->findOne('identities', [
         Query::equal('providerEmail', [$email]),
     ]);
     if (!$identityWithMatchingEmail->isEmpty()) {
         if (!$isVerified) {
             $failureRedirect(Exception::GENERAL_BAD_REQUEST);
         }
-        $user->setAttributes($dbForProject->getDocument('users', $identityWithMatchingEmail->getAttribute('userId'))->getArrayCopy());
+        $userFromIdentity = $dbForProject->getDocument('users', $identityWithMatchingEmail->getAttribute('userId'));
+        if (!$userFromIdentity->isEmpty()) {
+            $user->setAttributes($userFromIdentity->getArrayCopy());
+        }
     }
 }
```
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
            // If user is not found, check if there is an identity with the same email
            if ($user === false || $user->isEmpty()) {
                $identityWithMatchingEmail = $dbForProject->findOne('identities', [
                    Query::equal('providerEmail', [$email]),
                ]);
                if (!$identityWithMatchingEmail->isEmpty()) {
                    if (!$isVerified) {
                        $failureRedirect(Exception::GENERAL_BAD_REQUEST);
                    }
                    $userFromIdentity = $dbForProject->getDocument('users', $identityWithMatchingEmail->getAttribute('userId'));
                    if (!$userFromIdentity->isEmpty()) {
                        $user->setAttributes($userFromIdentity->getArrayCopy());
                    }
                }
            }
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In app/controllers/api/account.php around lines 1666 to 1677, the code calls
$user->setAttributes() with the result of $dbForProject->getDocument('users',
...) without checking that the fetched user document is non-empty; fetch the
document into a variable first, check isEmpty() on that document and only call
$user->setAttributes() when it contains data, otherwise treat it as a missing
user (e.g., call failureRedirect(Exception::GENERAL_BAD_REQUEST) or leave $user
empty) so an orphaned identity cannot set an empty attribute array onto $user
and bypass later isEmpty() checks.
```

</details>

